  "notes": "A replayed kit at 95 with the backbeat hard on 2 and 4, the kick answering itself on the and-of-2, and the hats shuffled just under the MPC setting — tambourine, shaker and conga carry the colour, and there is no 808 anywhere, because this is a sampled and live-replayed record. What makes it itself is the pair of portamento parts: a whiny high synth lead sitting up at C5–C7, and a Moog-style bass walking its own figure instead of mirroring the kick, both sliding between notes rather than stepping. Under them a two-to-four chord minor vamp with pentatonic and blues colour, sevenths and ninths present but never the point.",
